{
  "name": "exp_b_fair_convergence",
  "_doc": "Exp B (fair convergence) — AR vs PS under EQUAL WORKERS. AR runs N workers; PS runs the SAME N workers plus 2 sharded servers (servers are PS's own overhead, not a worker handicap). With equal workers and equal per-worker batch (10), the effective global batch (N x 10) is identical for AR and PS at each N, so convergence is directly comparable. Primary dataset FashionMNIST (harder, less homogeneous), MNIST kept for reference. batch 10/worker, lr 0.1, 30 epochs, eval on full test set.",
